# The derived STM32 pinout/spec index RAW sqlite (config_dir()/stm/index.sqlite by default,
# stays per-machine; the COMMITTED artifact is the compressed seed at data/stm/index.sqlite.xz,
# outside the repo already; these are belt-and-suspenders for any in-repo fallback path)
/.stockroom-stm-index/
*.stm-index.sqlite
# Derived Altium data sources, regenerated from the JSON records. NEITHER is committed.
# The .DbLib was committed until 2026-07-26, on the premise that it is portable. It is not: its
# ConnectionString names the SQLite file by an ABSOLUTE path (the SQLite ODBC driver resolves a
# relative one against the process working directory, which is never the library folder, so Altium
# answers it with "Connection Failed"). A committed copy is therefore one machine's file, and the
# one in this repo had gone stale in exactly that way: it still carried the broken relative form
# AND no key field, so a fresh clone got a library that connects to nothing and indexes nothing.
# The .db was committed until 2026-07-25 so a fresh clone was placeable with no regenerate step.
# That traded one benefit for a worse problem: SQLite stamps its own library version into the file
# header, so two peers on different SQLite builds emit different bytes for identical content, and
# two peers adding different parts produce genuinely unmergeable binaries carrying nothing the
# records do not already hold. LibraryOps.ensure_altium_datasource now rebuilds it on boot and on
# every profile switch, which keeps a fresh clone placeable without sharing the file.
libraries/*/altium/*.xlsx
libraries/*/altium/stockroom-parts.db
libraries/*/altium/*.DbLib

# Agent tooling: installed skills + SuperDesign workspace (never committed)
.agents/
.superdesign/
/skills-lock.json

